# Target C-II — the reflection outer-face inactive corridor is strictly support-monotone

**Date:** 2026-09-17  
**Status:** proved candidate awaiting promotion; proof-only strengthening of the outer-face inactive corridor  
**Scope:** parent chains generated by the FREE-module inactive-guard absorption process  
**Dependencies:** linear inactive-chain theorem; FREE-blocker outer-face theorem  
**Certificate:** `research/verify_target_c_tooth_reflection_outer_corridor_monotonicity_2026_09_17.py`  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The parent chain produced by the FREE repair has a directional property not used in the linear-length argument. Every new guard is hit for the **first** time by a point moving in direction `-N`. First-contact kinematics forces the contact vector to have nonnegative `N` projection. When translated back to the original source, the parent-to-child edge therefore has strictly positive inward support-depth increment.

Thus the macroscopic outer-face corridor is not merely a long path. It is a strictly `N`-monotone simple polygonal path:

\[
\boxed{
a_{z_0}<a_{z_1}<\cdots<a_{z_\ell}.}
\tag{MC.1}

Equivalently, orienting every edge from parent to child,

\[
\boxed{
N\cdot(z_j-z_{j+1})>0.
}
\tag{MC.2}

Its total inward projected length is exactly

\[
\boxed{
\sum_{j=0}^{\ell-1}N\cdot(z_j-z_{j+1})
=a_{z_\ell}-a_{z_0}
>\lambda D-O(\sqrt D).
}
\tag{MC.3}

So the surviving FREE geometry is a directed macroscopic corridor across the outer contact face, with no backtracking in the canonical blocker-normal coordinate.

---

## 1. First-contact derivative

Suppose a parent vertex `p` joined the moving cluster at time `sigma`, and a still-fixed inactive source point `v` is first met at time `s>sigma`.

Put

\[
\tau=s-\sigma>0
\]

and let

\[
c=p-\tau N-v
\]

be the unit contact vector at the event. Thus

\[
|c|=1.
\tag{MC.4}

Before the event, the child `v` is fixed while the parent moves with velocity `-N`. Define

\[
f(t)=|p-(t-\sigma)N-v|^2.
\]

For `t<s`, first-contact minimality gives

\[
f(t)>1,
\qquad
f(s)=1.
\]

Therefore the left derivative at `s` satisfies

\[
f'(s^-)\le0.
\]

But

\[
f'(s^-)=-2N\cdot c.
\]

Hence

\[
\boxed{N\cdot c\ge0.}
\tag{MC.5}

This remains valid at a tangential first contact, where equality may occur.

---

## 2. Original support depth increases strictly

Let

\[
a_w=H-N\cdot w
\]

be original-source support depth. Since

\[
p-v=c+\tau N,
\]

we have

\[
\begin{aligned}
a_v-a_p
&=N\cdot(p-v)\\
&=N\cdot c+\tau.
\end{aligned}
\]

Using (MC.5) and `tau>0`,

\[
\boxed{
a_v-a_p\ge\tau>0.}
\tag{MC.6}

Thus every parent edge makes strict inward progress in the canonical support coordinate.

Applied recursively to the ancestry chain,

\[
a_{z_0}<a_{z_1}<\cdots<a_{z_\ell},
\]

which proves (MC.1).

The same identity gives

\[
N\cdot(z_j-z_{j+1})
=a_{z_{j+1}}-a_{z_j}>0,
\]

which is (MC.2).

---

## 3. Exact projected-length ledger

Summing the edge projections telescopes:

\[
\begin{aligned}
\sum_{j=0}^{\ell-1}N\cdot(z_j-z_{j+1})
&=\sum_{j=0}^{\ell-1}(a_{z_{j+1}}-a_{z_j})\\
&=a_{z_\ell}-a_{z_0}.
\end{aligned}
\]

The linear-chain theorem gives

\[
a_{z_\ell}>\lambda D,
\qquad
a_{z_0}=O(\sqrt D),
\]

so

\[
\boxed{
\sum_{j=0}^{\ell-1}N\cdot(z_j-z_{j+1})
>\lambda D-O(\sqrt D).
}
\tag{MC.7}

There is no cancellation: all summands are positive.

---

## 4. The polygonal chain is geometrically simple

Parameterize each parent segment linearly in chain order. Equation (MC.2) says the support-depth coordinate `a=H-N dot x` increases strictly along the interior of every segment and across every vertex.

Hence every support line perpendicular to `N` meets the polygonal chain in at most one point. In particular the chain cannot self-intersect.

Therefore

\[
\boxed{
\text{the inactive corridor is an }N\text{-monotone simple polygonal arc.}
}
\tag{MC.8}

Combined with the outer-face theorem, this arc is embedded entirely in the unbounded face of the positive contact graph.

---

## 5. Frontier effect

The non-exact reflection endpoint is now

```text
one canonical support direction N
one outer-face inactive chain
strictly increasing N-depth from O(sqrt D) to lambda D
Omega(D) distinct old fully inactive vertices
every original edge in (1, 1.334748+o(1))
no contact-edge crossings
no self-crossings
projected inward length lambda D-O(sqrt D)
```

This monotonicity rules out explanations based on a long rattler chain that merely meanders tangentially while making negligible net inward progress. The remaining obstruction must realize a genuinely macroscopic directed corridor through the outer contact face.

**Disposition:** proved strict support-depth monotonicity and exact positive projected-length accumulation along the reflection-induced inactive parent chain. C-II remains open.
